WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.700
In Lahore's electronics markets, two similar-
looking parts may have very different

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.105
quality, warranties, and prices. TrustMart
helps a buyer inspect those differences

00:00:08.105 --> 00:00:09.440
before deciding.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:14.525
First, describe the component precisely. A
phone model, component type, quality

00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:18.130
grade, and warranty define the comparison
group. A cheaper but different

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.425
part is not automatically a better offer.

00:00:20.755 --> 00:00:24.130
The price engine keeps approved offers from
verified suppliers, with stock

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.540
available and timestamps no older than seven
days. A revoked, stale,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.565
or unavailable offer cannot influence this
calculation.

00:00:31.895 --> 00:00:34.890
With five or more eligible offers, it removes
twenty percent from

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.610
each end of the sorted prices, then averages
the remaining values.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.865
Smaller samples use the ordinary mean and
show low confidence.

00:00:42.195 --> 00:00:44.500
A camera scan or manual Shop I D resolves
through the

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.805
backend to the current supplier record.
Verified describes that record. It

00:00:48.805 --> 00:00:52.280
does not prove every product is authentic or
guarantee compensation.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:57.350
Customers can inspect disclosures, supplier
status, and report a problem. Suppliers

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:01.315
and administrators have separate permissions.
This demo uses fictional shops and

00:01:01.315 --> 00:01:05.155
sample prices, making its limits visible
alongside its features.
